  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far identifies scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted (config_031, 0.678 acc) as the best configuration, with scvi_n200 providing a large jump over pca_n2000 (+3.9%). The remaining uncertainty is whether a stronger image encoder (imagenet_vit_l vs resnet50) could further complement the scvi_n200 representation—the prior evidence is weak (only 0.4% difference with pca_n2000, config_019 vs config_025). config_037 isolates this single variable (image encoder) while holding all other proven-optimal settings fixed (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted fusion). This is the best use of the next budget slot because it exploits the strongest known direction while resolving a genuinely uncertain design choice; a positive result would immediately identify a new best configuration, and a null/negative result would confirm resnet50 suffices, freeing subsequent experiments to explore other axes (e.g., scgpt encoder or transformer aggregation)."
}

